==English==

===Etymology===
* From {{affix|en|ab-|articulation}}.
* Compare French ''abarticulation''. See [[article]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/æb.ɑɹˌtɪk.jʊˈleɪ.ʃən/|/æb.ɑˌtɪk.jʊˈleɪ.ʃən/|/æb.ɑɹˌtɪk.jəˈleɪ.ʃən/|/æb.ɑˌtɪk.jəˈleɪ.ʃən/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-abarticulation.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪʃən|s=6}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} An [[articulation]], especially one that permits free motion in the joint; a hinge joint.
# The act of [[dislocating]] a [[joint]].<ref>{{cite-book|editor=Thomas, Clayton L.|title=Taber's Encyclopedic Medical Dictionary|year=1940|edition=5th|year_published=1993|publisher=F. A. Davis Company|location=Philadelphia, PA|isbn=0-8036-8313-8|pages=1}}</ref>
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} A term sometimes used for [[diarthrosis]], and also for [[synarthrosis]]. Also called [[dearticulation]].

